' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
'   description:  UAF strict-grid (cells labeled by viewpoint x aspect) vs freeform layout.
'   usecase:      Teach when the UAF grid addressability matters vs a freeform sketch.
'   complexity:   variant
'   domain:       enterprise / defense-architecture
' ============================================================================
title Example UAF/UPDM - Grid vs Freeform

note as TopNote
  Variant: same 4-node surveillance story shown TWO ways.
  LEFT: strict UAF grid - each cell is addressed (row, col).
  RIGHT: freeform - same nodes/edges, no grid cells.
  Grid MATTERS when you need to prove viewpoint coverage or
  map each element to a canonical cell for tooling/traceability.
end note

' ============ LEFT: STRICT GRID ============
package "GRID: Operational x Activities" as G_OA {
  usecase "Conduct Patrol" as GA1
}

package "GRID: Operational x Resources" as G_OR {
  actor "Patrol Crew" as GP1
}

package "GRID: Systems x Resources" as G_SR {
  node "Radar" as GS1
}

package "GRID: Standards x Profiles" as G_SP {
  rectangle "STD: Link 22" as GST1
}

GP1 --> GA1 : performs
GA1 ..> GS1 : needline
GS1 ..> GST1 : conforms

' ============ RIGHT: FREEFORM (no grid cells) ============
actor "Patrol Crew (FF)" as FP1
usecase "Conduct Patrol (FF)" as FA1
node "Radar (FF)" as FS1
rectangle "STD: Link 22 (FF)" as FST1

FP1 --> FA1 : performs
FA1 --> FS1 : supported-by
FS1 --> FST1 : conforms
